  "knownLimitations": [
    "Release Git Tags contain SSH signatures; GitHub reports unknown_key until the public signing key is registered.",
    "Preview 7 qualification exposed Stage 9 test-harness defects: the guest-smoke IPC scan reads Gradle/JDK binaries as text; the workspace-lifecycle gate hardcodes the historical guigatedelta fixture; and its runClient readiness predicate can accept a surviving NeoForge initialization-error window as stable. The exact candidate's install/start IPC path was separately checked against real text logs, and its workspace generation plus Gradle build/JAR succeeded, but the Hyper-V guest cannot prove graphical runClient readiness because it exposes no usable OpenGL profile. Script fixes are deferred until after exact-binary promotion so the frozen candidate-to-Beta delta stays evidence/status/docs only.",
    "The real JCEF accessibility pass is not complete; the Hyper-V guest cannot validate Chromium WebContents accessibility because native Edge reproduces the same missing web-control subtree, so a physical or otherwise known-good Windows accessibility environment is required.",
    "The current Beta scope explicitly excludes the real JCEF accessibility audit, a graphics-capable clean-Windows runClient replay, and the external tester trial; those exclusions are not claims that the omitted checks passed. Preview 7 did complete the Stage 11 candidate-required Windows install/upgrade/uninstall, offline workspace launch, data-retention, provenance, and asset-verification replay.",
    "Windows packages are not Authenticode signed."
  ]
